## Email

`services/email.py`. In an endpoint, `sender: EmailSenderDep`, then
`await sender.send(OutgoingEmail(to=..., subject=..., text=...))`. For
anything not urgent, send it from a background task instead. Locally
`docker compose up` runs Mailpit: every email appears at
http://localhost:8025. In production set `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`,
`SMTP_USERNAME`, `SMTP_PASSWORD`, `SMTP_START_TLS` and `EMAIL_FROM`. Tests
read what was sent from the `outbox` fixture.
